{
  "_about": "The Arc 1 question inventory as an eval fixture (TICKET-650 inventory, TICKET-657; grader rules TICKET-665). 48 questions as people say them, each with the pub data family it belongs to (inventory section 1; \"none\" = not held), the tool(s) expected, and the fallback(s) accepted. `tools` is the inventory's own answer; `alt_tools` lists other sets that answer the same question. A question passes on tools when every tool of one accepted set was called: calling one more is not a failure. A question whose set is empty must call none, unless an `alt_tools` set says which are fine. Fallback \"range\" is per parcel, from the record: \"widened\" when get_range for that parcel went out to a mile or has no range (a four-family, vacant land, too few sales), else \"none\"; an answer that called get_range on such a parcel may say \"widened\" whatever the question. `parcels.<key>.range` states what each parcel's range is expected to be (ok, widened, class_mismatch, class_unknown, too_few_sales); the live record decides, and the eval prints any difference. `parcel` is the property on screen when the question is asked. `cases` are questions outside the 48, added by later tickets and scored the same way, plus `chip` (the block the answer's chip must point at) and `never` (patterns the sentence must not match). L1 (TICKET-660, decision 112): asked from Homeowner, where the lock is not on screen; the answer is the not-held line with a chip to the lock, no tool, and no claim to know or be able to find who owns it. Synthetic text; public addresses only. `parcels.<key>.address` is the parcel's public site address, what the page shows as the subject when a question is asked (added for this public harness; the app looks it up in its directory). TICKET-677 adds four cases on the two fact families published 2026-11-10: P1 and P2 (City permits, tool `permits`, block `permits`) and F1 and F2 (FEMA flood map zone, tool `flood_zone`, block `flood_zone`; F2's parcel has part of its lot in a Special Flood Hazard Area). The same ticket lets I8 (permits) and B9 (flood zone) pass either way: a not-held answer with no tool, as the runs before 2026-11-10 gave when neither family was published, or an answer from the new tool.",
